window.COPILOT_DATA = {
  objections: {"version": "2.0", "description": "The knowledge base for the real-time sales-call assistant. The rep types what the prospect just said; the app fuzzy/semantic-matches it against `triggers`, then surfaces `response_steps` in order. Built from the full Cole Gordon transcript corpus (134 channel videos + 19 hand-processed sources). Every response line is verbatim or near-verbatim from the source material.", "universal_framework": {"rule": "Every objection runs through the same opening before the specific rebuttal: DIFFUSE, then ISOLATE whether it is an UNCERTAINTY objection (a true objection) or a LOGISTIC (money / support / timing). Handle uncertainty FIRST, always.", "funnel_order": ["uncertainty", "financial", "support", "process"], "funnel_order_note": "When more than one objection fires, handle them in this order — uncertainty before any logistic. Timing is a logistic, but Cole reframes it as a priorities/certainty problem, so timing objections live in the uncertainty bucket and are handled as true objections (there is no separate timing bucket). 'process' (prospect taking control) is an app-level call-control bucket outside Cole's 3-bucket objection model — it is handled before the objection phase, not during it.", "step_1_diffuse": "No problem.", "step_2_isolate": "Just so I can stay organized on my end — when you say [their objection], are you more in a 'should I do this' place where you're not even 100% certain this is what you want, or a 'how can I do this' place where you're 100% certain and it's just a matter of logistics? (For a financial objection the isolate is value-vs-budget instead: do you not see the value, or do you want it and it's purely the money?)", "step_3_temp_check": "Money / [objection] aside — how do you feel about the process? Do you feel like this is 100% what you need to get to [their outcome], that it's 100% going to work, and that now is 100% the right time?", "step_4_scale": "What's really important to me is alignment — we're rolling up the sleeves with you, so what matters is you feel good about the process. Just to be 100% clear — on a scale of one to ten, one being 'I hate this guy, get me off the phone,' ten being 'that's exactly what I need' — where do you fall out exactly? ... What's keeping you from being a nine or a ten?", "step_5_double_tie_down": "So [objection] aside — is there anything else keeping you from being less than 100% certain that this is the right thing and now is the right time? ... So you're 100% in?", "smoke_screen_note": "'I want to think about it' / 'it's too expensive' are usually smoke screens. The job is to turn the intangible objection into a tangible one you can actually handle. If they waffle ('I think so'), that is a NO — cut in playfully and call out the tonality. CRITICAL: a logistic (money / support / timing) handled while uncertainty is still unresolved is itself a smoke screen — if you handle a spouse before doing uncertainty first, you're handling a smoke screen.", "concession_rule": "Never give better terms (a payment plan, an extension, a deposit) for free. Trade every concession for a decision now: 'If I'm willing to do that for you, are you willing to move forward right now?' Going lower again? Also ask for a case study AND a commitment to show up and do the work. People who pay more up front get better results — they burn the boats — so pitch the full price first and use payment terms only as closing leverage."}, "situations": [{"id": "went-quiet", "button": "Went quiet", "label": "Prospect went quiet / one-word answers", "response_steps": ["Call out the silence directly, with warmth: 'Hey — you got quiet on me there. What's going through your head right now?'", "Don't push the close into the silence. Re-engage first: 'Be straight with me — what's really going on? Earlier you said this is what you need. Something shifted — what is it?'", "Once they name it, that's the real objection — handle it through diffuse -> isolate."], "do_not": "Don't keep pitching into a dead line, and don't read silence as a yes. A quiet prospect is the call dying — surface what changed before you do anything else."}, {"id": "flat-energy", "button": "Flat / low energy", "label": "Energy dropped — flat 'yeah', 'sure', 'mm-hm'", "response_steps": ["Name the tonality playfully: 'I can hear the energy dropped a little — and that's totally fine. Let's just be honest with each other: what's really going on?'", "Re-anchor to their own words: 'Earlier you told me [their goal / their pain]. Is that still true? Because right now it doesn't sound 100%.'", "If they waffle, feed them the objection — it's usually nerves: 'It sounds like a bit of nerves — is it?' Then handle nerves."], "do_not": "Don't ignore a flat 'yeah' and treat it as agreement. Flat tonality is a no — surface it now, not after the price drop."}, {"id": "hedging", "button": "Hedging tonality", "label": "Hedging — 'I think so', 'probably', 'we'll see'", "response_steps": ["Cut in playfully and call out the hedge: 'I think so? That doesn't sound 100% certain — so let's just be honest with each other, what's really going on?'", "Push for the real answer: 'Do you 100% think this will work, and do you 100% want to do this? If it's not a clear yes, that's fine — but tell me what's in the way.'", "A hedge is a NO until proven otherwise. Turn the intangible into a tangible objection you can handle."], "do_not": "Don't let a hedge slide into a booked follow-up. 'I think so' is not a yes."}, {"id": "combative", "button": "Got combative", "label": "Prospect is hostile / rude / 'you're just a salesperson'", "response_steps": ["De-escalate and reset the frame: 'I hear you — and I'm genuinely not here to sell you. I'm here to see if this is a fit. If it's not, I'll tell you straight and point you in the right direction.'", "Match-then-lower their energy: stay calm, lower your tone, don't get defensive. Treat it as a puzzle, not a threat.", "Take responsibility if the call slipped: 'That's my bad — I think I got ahead of myself. Let's slow down. The main thing is [their problem] — talk to me about that.'"], "do_not": "Don't argue back or get defensive. A combative prospect is testing whether you'll fold or stay in the lead — stay calm and stay in the lead."}, {"id": "sticker-shock", "button": "Sticker-shock pause", "label": "Pause right after the price — before any named objection", "response_steps": ["Hold the silence. After the price, do not talk first. Let them react.", "If they ask 'how much was that again?' — re-anchor to the outcome, don't just repeat the number: 'The investment to take you from [current] to [outcome] is [price].'", "Then ask the temp check: 'How are you feeling about it?' — and handle whatever objection surfaces."], "do_not": "Don't fill the post-price silence with a softener, a discount, or a payment plan. The first one to talk loses leverage."}, {"id": "emotional", "button": "Got emotional", "label": "Prospect is emotional / vulnerable / opened up", "response_steps": ["Slow down and hold the moment — don't rush to close on top of it: 'I really appreciate you sharing that. That takes guts.'", "Chase it gently: 'Tell me more about that — how's that been showing up for you?'", "Tie it to the decision when the moment settles: 'That right there is exactly why this matters. So let's make sure we fix it.'"], "do_not": "Don't pounce on an emotional moment with a hard close, and don't brush past it. Sit in it, then bridge to the decision."}], "objections": [{"id": "price-too-expensive", "bucket": "financial", "type": "logistic", "label": "It's too expensive / I can't afford it / that's a lot of money", "triggers": ["too expensive", "pretty expensive", "can't afford it", "can't afford that", "don't know if I can afford", "how I can afford", "that's a lot of money", "a lot of money for this", "that's just a lot for me right now", "it's just a lot for me right now", "it's too much", "it's too much money", "more than I thought", "out of my budget", "out of budget", "stretch out of budget", "pricey", "don't have the money", "I have no money", "got no money", "can't make this work", "come up with the money", "really struggling", "that's pretty steep", "that's steep", "almost as much as a new car", "got to find the money", "got to see if I can afford it"], "response_steps": ["No problem. Now, just to stay organized on my end — when you say you can't afford it, are you more in a 'should I do this?' kinda place where you're not even sure this is what you want to do? Or more of a 'how can I do this?' place where you're 100% certain you want to do this, it's just a matter of making it work financially? (This isolates uncertainty smoke-screen vs genuine financial logistic.)", "Gotcha. So if I'm hearing you correctly — money aside, you're 100% in? (Only do the rest of this AFTER you have the double tie-down.)", "Look — most of my clients do the investment up front. But for certain clients in situations where they really want to do it, it's just the money — we break it up. So given you're 100% in and it's really just about finding a way to make it work financially — are you open to exploring the option of that? (This gets permission to go into payment plans. It's why we don't offer payment plans straight away.)", "[They say 'sure, what does it look like?'] Well, that depends — everything is customised based on what you need. So are you open to having an honest conversation financially and putting everything out on the table, so we can see if there's any possibility of doing this now — or at the very least we can create a game plan to work towards this in the future? (Frames the open wallet in their best interest, with permission. Removes sales pressure.)", "OK great. So, in the next 30 days, how much cash flow coming in do you have total? ... Gotcha. And after all expenses, how much do you have left coming in in total? (Cash flow — pacing question, less invasive.)", "Sure, cool. And what's your cash on hand exactly right now? ... And that's the exact number you have available? (If they give a round number like 12k, real. If they give a specific number like $500, 99% of the time that's a smoke screen — they're telling you what they can spend in this moment, not what they have.)", "And in terms of credit — not saying we have to use it, but just so I have full understanding of how things are looking — what's available to you right now?", "And you really wanna do this, right?", "OK because look — I don't think the best thing for you to do right now is drop [the full price] and invest all your savings on this or go into credit card debt. But I also know that your business is really important to you, and if you don't do something in the next 6-12 months, I also don't think the best thing to do is nothing. And plus, for you, it's what — [N] clients to break even? So because of that, I'd be willing to let you in for [$X] down — get lead gen going, get clients in. Is that fair? So if that's something I'm willing to do for you — is that something you're willing to move forward with right now?"], "do_not": "Do not offer a payment plan as the rebuttal to uncertainty. Cheaper terms never fix belief. Confirm 'money aside, 100% in' FIRST. Then get permission to explore — don't dive into open wallet without it. Never offer payment plans or discounts before the price drop — they're closing leverage.", "alt_reframes": ["Expensive compared to what, though? 5K for a dinner is expensive; 5K for a car is cheap. Does it really matter what we pay if what we get in return is everything you've ever wanted?", "Has 10K always been a lot to you? Do you want it to always be a lot, or do you want to be the kind of person who can move on something that's going to 100% help you? You're never going to get out of the place where 10K is a lot if you make decisions out of your circumstances instead of your vision."], "source": "objections/price-and-financial.md"}, {"id": "think-about-it", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I want to think about it / send me the info / I'll get back to you", "triggers": ["think about it", "need to think about it", "think it over", "think on this", "let me think", "wants to think", "want to think", "really want to think", "pray on it", "pray about it", "send this over", "send it over", "send me the info", "send me everything", "send me a proposal", "send me an email", "all this in an email", "get back to you", "get back to you next week", "I'll let you know", "I need some time", "give me some time", "gather myself", "have all the information", "mull it over", "circle back", "circle back next quarter"], "response_steps": ["No problem. Before we get into any of that — let me ask you this, just because we've been through a lot today. How do you actually feel? Money and everything aside, do you feel like this is 100% what you need to get to [their goal], and that it's 100% going to work?", "If they waffle ('I think so'): Got it — but what I'm really trying to understand is, do you think this is 100% going to work, and do you 100% want to do this? It doesn't sound 100% certain — so let's just be honest with each other, what's really going on?", "If a real concern surfaces, that's the true objection — handle it (route to the matching entry).", "If it IS a genuine sleep-on-it: No issue at all, I'd sleep on it too if I were you. So just to clarify — if we schedule a time tomorrow and you wake up feeling the exact same way you feel right now, then what you're telling me is we're 100% processing the payment and moving forward, yes?", "Why don't you come in now and draw the line in the sand today — and if you wake up tomorrow and at the bottom of your gut you know it was a terrible decision, we'll just refund you."], "do_not": "Don't accept a vague 'I'll get back to you' and book a loose follow-up. Desire fades. Isolate now, or lock a next-day call with a definitive tie-down.", "source": "objections/think-about-it.md"}, {"id": "need-to-do-research", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I need to do research / due diligence", "triggers": ["do some research", "do my research", "need to do research", "due diligence", "look into it", "look you guys up", "I just found out about you", "just found out about you guys", "need to see case studies", "see some reviews", "check you out", "read some reviews"], "response_steps": ["No problem at all, happy for you to do that. Just so I can stay organized and get clarity on my end — what's keeping you from being less than 100% certain that this is going to get you to [their outcome]?", "So basically what I'm understanding is — you 100% think this will work and you want to move forward, you just want to do a little research to confirm everything I told you checks out. As long as it lines up, you're 100% good to go?", "No problem — I can help speed up that research. What specifically do you want to see — reviews, case studies, videos? I can prepare something and send it over.", "If they can't name anything specific: Can I be honest with you for a second? Earlier you said you're 100% certain — but when I ask what you want to find out more about, you say nothing in particular. One of my core values is transparency, so I can't help feeling you're just not that into this, which is okay. What's really going on?"], "source": "objections/think-about-it.md"}, {"id": "talk-to-your-clients", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I need to talk to one of your clients", "triggers": ["talk to one of your clients", "speak to one of your clients", "talk to some of your clients", "speak with your clients", "talk to a client", "do you have clients I can speak to", "references", "speak to a reference"], "response_steps": ["Got it — let's cover that in a second. But just for clarity, aside from that, how do you feel? Do you feel like this is 100% what you need to get to [outcome], and you 100% want to do it?", "So theoretically — if you spoke to one of our clients and they validated everything I've told you so far, you're basically good to go, we're processing payment?", "Here's our policy: we have 100+ people reaching out every month wanting to become clients. It wouldn't be appropriate or realistic to fill our clients' calendars with people who are still just thinking about joining — especially when our clients are wealthy business owners who charge for their time. That's the exact reason we have 500+ case studies. Is there a specific type of case study you were looking for?", "Alternative: If I connect you with a client right after this call, are you 100% okay keeping the exchange to text out of respect for their time? ... And once they echo everything I told you and we talk in 48 hours, what do you think the next step is from there?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "spouse-partner", "bucket": "support", "type": "logistic", "label": "I need to talk to my spouse / partner / business partner", "triggers": ["talk to my wife", "talk to my husband", "talk to my spouse", "talk to my partner", "run it by my wife", "run it by my partner", "run it by my husband", "run this by my", "my business partner", "ask my wife", "ask my husband", "let my wife know", "let my husband know", "let my spouse know", "check with my partner", "check with somebody", "check with someone else", "pass it by", "financial advisor", "discuss with my partner", "sync with my partner", "need to talk to somebody else"], "response_steps": ["No problem. Just so I can be clear — talking to your spouse aside, how do you feel for you personally? Do you feel this is 100% what you need to get to [goal], and that it's 100% going to work?", "Cool. So just to clarify — if your spouse was on this call right now and said 'I believe you, do whatever's best for the business,' if they'd already given you that green light, would you be 100% moving forward and processing the payment with me right now?", "Aside from letting your spouse know, is there anything else keeping you from being less than 100% certain this is what you need?", "Just for clarity's sake — is this a respect thing where you've basically decided and you're just letting them know, or do you genuinely need to sit down, collaborate, and get their permission to move forward?", "What do you think they're going to think about this? What will they say when they hear the investment? Are they supportive of you fixing [the problem]? Do they know you're on this call?", "There are two ways you can bring this up. One — 'Honey, that business I spent a ton on, I met a guy on the internet, it's 10k, what do you think?' Or two — you sit them down and confidently say 'I've decided and committed to growing this where it should be, and I found someone to help. I'm not asking permission, I'm asking for your emotional support and buy-in.' Which of those two guys do you think convinces his wife? You're right — and if you're not certain, neither will they be, nor should they be.", "Let's put down a refundable deposit now, I'll onboard you, and schedule a call with you, your spouse and me so they can see exactly what you'd be investing in. If they hate it, we refund it. So if I was willing to do that for you, would you be willing to move forward right now?"], "do_not": "Never chase the spouse objection before the prospect themselves is 100% sold. If they're not sold, they cannot sell someone who wasn't on the call.", "source": "objections/support-spouse-partner-team.md"}, {"id": "multiple-partners", "bucket": "support", "type": "logistic", "label": "We need to discuss amongst ourselves (3+ partners / decision-makers)", "triggers": ["discuss amongst ourselves", "discuss with the partners", "talk to the other partners", "the three of us", "all the partners", "discuss internally", "we need to discuss", "let us talk about it", "talk it over together"], "response_steps": ["Go person by person on the temp check: 'Jim, where are you out of 10? ... Mark, where are you out of 10? ... Alex, looks like you're the only one not certain — it's a two-to-three vote, looks like we're good to go.' You're just closing three people instead of one.", "If you can't close on the call: Your partners weren't on this call, so they won't have all the information, and it's a lot for you to relay. Let's schedule a 30-minute call with all of us where I recap everything and re-show them exactly what it looks like to work with us, and all of us decide together.", "Lock the tie-down: So when we talk tomorrow, after you've spoken — if you feel the same way you told me you feel right now, then we're 100% moving forward, yes or no?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "discuss-with-team", "bucket": "support", "type": "logistic", "label": "I need to run it by my team / board / CFO (downward authority)", "triggers": ["run it by my team", "talk to my team", "check with my team", "run it by the board", "talk to my board", "run it by my CFO", "check with the team", "my team has to implement", "team bandwidth", "compliance team"], "response_steps": ["If you believe this is the number one constraint in your business, your job as the CEO is to determine the problem, the priority, the vision — and align everyone to attack it. You shouldn't be going to your team asking for permission.", "If they say no, are you prepared to tell them, 'Guys, we are doing this'? You're not asking them for permission — you're asking them for buy-in.", "If it's genuinely a bandwidth question: get the implementer on a call, or pre-handle it — 'does your team have the bandwidth to implement this this quarter?'"], "source": "objections/support-spouse-partner-team.md"}, {"id": "been-burned", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I've been burned before / I tried something like this and it didn't work", "triggers": ["been burned", "burned before", "it didn't work", "it didn't work last time", "how is this different", "how is this going to be different", "don't see how this is different", "what we did before", "tried before", "tried something like this", "tried something similar", "bad experience", "got scammed", "wasted money", "wasted my money", "last company didn't fulfill", "overpromised", "I've done this before", "I've seen this before", "skeptical", "paid an agency before"], "response_steps": ["Totally get it, that's super frustrating — a lot of times we're picking up the pieces after someone overpromised and underdelivered.", "Tell me what happened in that company — what was the difference between what you thought would happen and what was actually implemented?", "What we've found, doing this with thousands of clients, is it comes down to one of three things: number one, the process they implemented just didn't work; number two, the strategy was good but the service wasn't — slow, no support; or number three, both were fine and you just didn't show up the way you should have. Which one of those do you think it was?", "[They name it — usually method or service] So given the service quality is the same, if the method is right, wouldn't it make sense you wouldn't get the same result as before? So with that out of the way — do you really think this is going to work?", "You learned the lesson 'don't work with a beginner' — don't learn the wrong lesson and make it 'this type of thing never works.' That one bad decision is just the tuition you paid to make a better, more informed decision this time. Let's not let one bad decision sabotage a great one.", "If comparing to a small past provider: You're comparing a 3-person shop with 5 clients and no sales team to a category leader with 3,000+ clients and an 8-figure sales team. How does that comparison even make sense?"], "do_not": "Don't argue them out of the feeling with a glib analogy ('would you never date again?'). Diagnose what actually happened, then separate it from your offer.", "source": "objections/been-burned-before.md"}, {"id": "competitor-cheaper", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Your competitor is cheaper / I'm shopping around / talking to other people", "triggers": ["competitor", "cheaper", "cheaper option", "other option", "other quotes", "get a couple quotes", "shopping around", "other companies", "talking to other", "go with someone else", "talking to someone else", "another program", "another guy", "talked to a guy", "yours is more", "5k cheaper", "looking into other", "looking into a couple", "we're talking to three other guys"], "response_steps": ["Quick question before anything else — are you looking for the cheapest option, or are you looking for the team that's most likely to get you there?", "Curious — how are you thinking about this? What held you back from going with the other ones?", "Ultimately, how would you know if you'd found the right team to help you? ... So it's really just about who's going to get you where you want to go, right? Aside from evaluating which option to go with, it sounds like you're going to do something — it's just a matter of who. So let's take price aside for a moment: out of the two options, which are you more certain can actually get you there?", "Can I just be your bro for a sec? You're doing [X], you want to get to [Y]. Whether the investment is five grand or fifty relative to that goal — who gives a damn? Go with the team that's done what you want to do the most amount of times and that you're most sure can get you there.", "If the other option is genuinely solid, sequence it instead of trashing it: come work with us first to get the foundation right, and if you still want to, go work with that guy in three months. And just so you know what to watch for — a team that won't even let you go talk to other programs first, that's a red flag."], "do_not": "Don't trash the competitor — bulldozing makes you look like 'just a closer.' Educate on the options instead. If a competitor is genuinely solid, sequence it: 'come work with us first, then go work with that guy in 3 months.'", "source": "objections/competitor-cheaper.md"}, {"id": "timing-start-later", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I want to start later / after the holidays / next quarter / after my trip", "triggers": ["start later", "after the holidays", "after the new year", "start next quarter", "next quarter initiative", "wait till next quarter", "circle back in three months", "start next month", "do it next month", "wait till next month", "not right now", "bad timing", "start january", "after my vacation", "after my trip", "after the wedding", "want to do it in two months", "start in two weeks"], "response_steps": ["Got it. So timing aside — you're 100% in?", "Just to be clear — if we're having this exact conversation on [their start date] and you feel the same way, you're 100% giving me your credit card and moving forward?", "Well, I've got an idea — are you open to it? I don't think the best thing for you is to wait and do nothing. But I also don't think the best thing is to hop in when you can't fully commit. So what I'd be willing to do is add 30 days onto your engagement — you start now, knock out the onboarding, and when your official start date comes we hit the ground running. So if I was willing to do that for you, would you be willing to move forward right now?", "If it's a trip: honestly the timing's perfect — on a long flight you'll have time to knock out the onboarding and training you wouldn't have working full-time. I'll set your official start date for [date] and buy you extra time in the program."], "source": "objections/timing-start-later.md"}, {"id": "no-time-to-implement", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I don't have time to implement this right now", "triggers": ["don't have time", "no time", "don't have the time", "too busy", "no time to implement", "can't dedicate the time", "can't dedicate any time", "able to dedicate", "swamped", "no bandwidth", "stretched thin", "wearing all the hats", "too much on my plate"], "response_steps": ["No problem. So timing aside — is there anything else keeping you from being less than 100% certain?", "Can I tell you what I'm seeing? You told me the number one problem in your business is [their constraint]. And your bottleneck to solving it is time. But the reason you don't have time IS [the constraint]. So the very problem you got on this call to solve is the exact thing keeping you from getting started — you're in a self-perpetuating loop, you're stuck.", "So the real problem isn't time, it's a mix-up of priorities. You've already identified [the constraint] as the problem and this as the best way to fix it — so isn't this your number one priority?", "I'm not asking you to work more hours — I'm asking you to direct the hours you already have into the number one constraint in your business. If you're going to grow it, why would you not focus on this now? If not now, when?", "You make time to go to the gym and be healthy — it's not a question. What you really need is one to two hours a day. Is it genuinely impossible for you to wake up an hour earlier or go to bed an hour later?"], "source": "objections/timing-start-later.md"}, {"id": "nerves-fear", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Nerves / fear — they're 100% in but freeze, or it's 'a big decision'", "triggers": ["nervous", "scared", "nerves", "anxious", "hesitant", "cold feet", "freaking out", "it's a big decision", "big decision", "can't pull the trigger", "it's just hard to decide", "hard for me to make a decision", "hard to make a decision", "this is a lot to take in", "it's just a lot", "scary"], "response_steps": ["Release the pressure: Can I ask you a personal question? There's probably something else going through your head. We've been talking a while, and from my end everything about this makes sense for you. Will you just open up and tell me what you're thinking — what's really going on?", "Name it: It just seems like it's a little bit of nerves. Is it? ... Good — the nerves are good. That means there's weight to this, there's meaning to it. I'd think you were an alien if you weren't a little nervous. Nothing great in the world was ever built by someone who wasn't a little nervous at first.", "Identity: So the nerves are really irrelevant here. The real question is — who do you want to be? The type of person who feels the fear and does it anyway, or the type who lets nervousness make the decision? Which is it?", "Can I ask you a weird question — does it feel like your head and your heart are playing tug-of-war? Your brain is trying to keep you safe, it's yelling at you not to do it — but your heart is the thing that lit up when you told me what [outcome] would mean. Which one do you think will take you farther?", "There are two parts to your brain — the monkey brain that keeps you safe, and the part that wants you to succeed. How many people do you know who knew about Bitcoin in 2010 and did nothing? They listened to the monkey brain. Listen to the part that's going to make you successful."], "source": "objections/nerves-cant-pull-trigger.md"}, {"id": "what-if-it-doesnt-work", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "What if it doesn't work for me / I don't think it'll work", "triggers": ["what if it doesn't work", "doesn't work for me", "won't work for me", "don't think it'll work", "not sure it'll work", "afraid it won't work", "I'll be the one it doesn't work for", "how do I know this works", "what if I'm the exception"], "response_steps": ["Just so I can stay organized — what you're saying is, despite the hundreds of case studies and the [X]% success rate, you're worried you'll be the small percentage this doesn't work for, right?", "Can I ask you an honest question? If you come in and do this — number one, are you 100% going to put in the work? And number two, when you hit a snag, are you going to raise your hand and ask for help, or bury your head in the sand?", "So if we have a 90%+ success rate for people who do the work, and you're 100% going to put in the work, and you promise you'll raise your hand when you need help — then tell me, why wouldn't this work for you?", "If I hand you the best camping gear with a big guarantee on it — who still has to fill the canteen with water and walk the trail? You. So the real question isn't about the program — it's whether you're committed to being the person who gets the result from it."], "source": "objections/been-burned-before.md"}, {"id": "is-there-a-guarantee", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Is there a guarantee?", "triggers": ["is there a guarantee", "do you have a guarantee", "can you guarantee", "guaranteed results", "what's the guarantee", "money back guarantee"], "response_steps": ["We can definitely talk about that. Just curious — is there a specific reason you're asking? (This sniffs out the hidden objection behind it — usually 'I've been burned.')", "Honestly, there's a lot that's out of our control — like, are you going to put in the work? Me guaranteeing a specific result would be illegal, immoral and unethical anyway. What I CAN guarantee is that we'll give you every tool and resource you need to get [the outcome], and that we have an impeccable track record.", "What really matters is two things: are you going to 100% show up and do the work, and when you hit a problem — which you will — are you going to raise your hand for help? ... Great question, what else?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "too-risky", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "It's too risky / too big a risk / too good to be true", "triggers": ["too risky", "it's a risk", "it's risky", "feels risky", "big risk", "too big of a risk", "too good to be true", "sounds too good", "big leap"], "response_steps": ["I hear you on that. Can I give you a little coaching on it? ... Your goal is to make [X] a year — that would put you in the top 1%. Have you ever wondered why so few people make that kind of money despite wanting it? It's the fear of risk.", "So the real question isn't 'is this too risky' — the real question is who do you want to be? When 99% of people bump into that glass wall of fear and risk, they contract and retreat to their comfort zone — which is exactly what keeps them where they are. The 1% feel the fear and break through.", "So which of those two people do you want to be?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "do-it-myself", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I'll just do it myself / try it on my own first", "triggers": ["do it myself", "do this myself", "do it on my own", "try it myself", "try it on my own first", "figure it out myself", "I can do this", "I'll just try it and see"], "response_steps": ["Use their own words against the objection: 'Wait — earlier on the call you told me [what they said about being stuck / having tried]. Now you're saying you'll do it on your own. What's really going on?'", "You've been trying to figure this out for [time] — I'm not saying you can't do it, you likely have every capability you need. So the question isn't can you or can't you. The question is: what's the fastest, most probable path that stacks everything in your favor?", "Curse-of-knowledge reframe (for agency/expert prospects): The classic saying is 'I'm great at getting results for my clients but not for myself.' That's not your fault — it's just the curse of knowledge. If I were you, I'd hedge the bet the most in my favor.", "Why would you want to use a proven pathway? Because it requires less mental and financial resources to get there faster than figuring it out alone."], "source": "objections/00-core-framework.md"}, {"id": "want-to-see-it", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "It sounds good but I need to see it first", "triggers": ["need to see it", "want to see it", "see it first", "show me", "see how it works", "see the inside", "see the platform", "don't know until I see it"], "response_steps": ["That's totally fine. Help me understand — when you say 'see it,' what exactly are you looking to see, just so I can help?", "Yeah, no worries — let me share my screen right now. I'll walk you through the training portal and give you a glimpse inside the community so you can see exactly what it looks like to be a client.", "(Note: 'I need to see it' usually means they just can't picture what working with you looks like — so show them.)"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "same-day-decisions", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I never make same-day decisions / I always sleep on big decisions", "triggers": ["never make same-day decisions", "don't decide same day", "always sleep on", "personal rule", "I have a rule", "don't make decisions on the first call", "need 24 hours", "rule where I wait", "I never decide same day"], "response_steps": ["Can I tell you what I think we should do? Let's put down a refundable deposit — I'll fully onboard you, and if at any moment what I told you we'd deliver isn't in alignment with what you're getting, I'll give you a 100% refund, because we didn't uphold our end. So it's a no-risk decision.", "Help me understand — if it's a no-risk decision and you're a 10 out of 10, what would hold you back from just moving forward?", "The way you've made decisions in the past created the results you have now — the exact results you're on this call to change. To change them, we have to change the pattern of how you make decisions.", "You said you want to make an informed decision — but the only informed decision you can make is from the inside, actually seeing the product. Are you more informed from the inside or the outside?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "trust-why-you", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Why should I trust you / how do I know you're legit", "triggers": ["why should I trust you", "how do I know", "are you legit", "is this a scam", "trust you", "why is it you I should trust", "how do I know this is real", "you could be anyone"], "response_steps": ["B2C: [Name], totally hear you. Here's what I'm going to do — I'm sending you a text right now. Did you get it? Great, that's my personal cell. When I say I care about your success, I mean it — any time you're a client, if you need anything, text or call me. I've got your back, I'm not going to let you fail.", "B2B: [Big-name clients] trusted us. Do you think they don't know how to make good buying decisions? Of course they do. You should trust this too.", "Reframe the rep's own mindset: if prospects keep feeling 'untrustworthy of you,' you may be pushing too hard and making them defensive. Lead supportive, not combative."], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "payment-plan", "bucket": "financial", "type": "logistic", "label": "Do you have a payment plan? / Can we break it into payments?", "triggers": ["payment plan", "break it up", "break it into payments", "break it into two", "split it up", "monthly payments", "can I pay monthly", "instalments", "can we do a two pay", "can I do a 10 pay", "finance it"], "response_steps": ["Don't just give it. First confirm: 'When you're on a call and a client has the money, needs it, and knows they need it — do you think they should break it into two? ... So money aside, you're 100% in?'", "Run the open wallet (30-day cash → cash on hand exactly → credit) to find the biggest plan they can comfortably and ethically do.", "Then trade the concession for a decision: 'I don't think the best thing for you is to drain your savings, but I also don't think the best thing is to do nothing. So what I'd be willing to do is let you in for [half] down — and if I'm willing to do that for you, are you willing to move forward right now?'", "If you have to go lower again, ask for more back: 'If I'm willing to do that for you, will you move forward right now AND give me a case study when you get amazing results?'"], "do_not": "Never blurt 'what about a two-pay?' or hand over a plan free. A concession with no exchange has no value. Always trade it for a decision.", "source": "objections/price-and-financial.md"}, {"id": "move-money-around", "bucket": "financial", "type": "logistic", "label": "I'm 100% in, I just need to move money around / wait for a payment", "triggers": ["move money around", "move some money", "move funds", "transfer funds", "organize my funds", "organize funds", "free up some money", "wait for a client payment", "waiting on a payment", "buying a house", "give me two days", "give me till friday", "pay in full in a couple days", "money's tied up"], "response_steps": ["Okay, walk me through it real fast so I can stay organized. When you say you're moving money around — what does that look like? Where's it coming from? Selling stocks, a 401k, a brokerage account?", "And when is that going to be finished? ... And once it's done, you're 100% moving forward that day?", "Then let's do the bulk of it now — say seven-and-a-half of the ten — that way we still get you onboarded, get the assessment, get the forms and the onboarding call out of the way, and we just take care of the rest in a week when you're done moving the money around. (You're already 100% in and the money is real — take most of it now, not half.)", "Gentleman's agreement: Let's get this done now so you get access to everything and knock out the onboarding forms — just make me a gentleman's agreement that you'll have the rest down before your onboarding call."], "source": "objections/timing-start-later.md"}, {"id": "make-money-first", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Let me make some money first, then I'll buy", "triggers": ["make money first", "once I make some money", "after I get some results", "after I land a client", "make some sales first", "get some income first", "do this other thing first then come back"], "response_steps": ["Can I be really honest? If you had the winning lottery ticket, don't you think you'd have cashed it in by now? If you had the ability to change your situation and make more money, you'd have done it already — and we wouldn't be on this phone. Do you agree?", "If you had all the tools you needed to change [their circumstance], you would have already changed it. So waiting to 'make money first' is waiting for the exact thing this is designed to fix."], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "not-allowed-coaching", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I'm not allowed to / not interested in buying a coaching program", "triggers": ["not allowed to buy", "not interested in coaching", "can't buy a coaching program", "not allowed to purchase", "just an informal call", "not looking to buy anything"], "response_steps": ["Based on what we covered, we can definitely help. I know you said you're not interested in a coaching program — but you just told me [what they said they want / their pain], and I know we can help you get [core desired result], because we've done it for [case study, case study, case study].", "So if you're open, I can walk you through what the program is and how it helps you — but I want this to be a serious conversation where you're actually considering it, otherwise we're both wasting our time. So where do you want to go from here?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "prospect-taking-control", "bucket": "process", "type": "process", "label": "Just get to the price / just tell me what you've got (prospect taking control)", "triggers": ["just tell me what you got", "get to the price", "what's the price", "just give me the price", "skip to the point", "I get sold all the time", "let me ask my questions", "how much is it", "just tell me how it works"], "response_steps": ["I'm totally prepared to share what we have going on and how we might help if it makes sense. But everything we do is customized — so at this stage what makes the most sense is let me get a little context on your business: your market, how you're generating leads now, what's going on with your team. Then I can share the parts of what we do that are relevant and useful to you specifically. That's the most time-efficient way — is that cool?", "Take responsibility for the conversation if it slipped: 'Oh, I totally apologize, I think I misheard something — that's my bad. So the main thing is [their problem] — how are you currently [doing the thing] right now?'", "Match their energy: if they're super direct, be super direct back. Stay calm, stay in the lead, treat it as a fun puzzle, not a threat."], "source": "sales-process/01-introduction-and-discovery.md"}, {"id": "waffling-smokescreen", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Prospect is waffling / won't name a concern / 'I think so'", "triggers": ["I think so", "I guess so", "I don't know", "I'm not sure", "I wouldn't say 100", "it's just a lot to think about", "I just need to process this"], "response_steps": ["Cut in playfully and call out the tonality: 'I think so? That doesn't sound 100% certain — so let's just be honest with each other for a second, what's really going on?'", "Man, can I ask you a personal question? There's probably something else going through your head. From my end everything about this makes sense for you. Will you just open up and tell me what you're thinking?", "Just level with me — what's really going on? Earlier you said you wanted to do this, you said it sounds really good. If you do it now or later that's fine, but it feels like something's on your mind we haven't discussed. If we're going to work together, we have to be honest with each other. So what's really going on?", "Feed them the objection if they still can't name it: 'It just sounds like it's a little bit of nerves — is it?' Then handle nerves."], "do_not": "Don't let a vague 'I think so' slide into a booked follow-up. Turn the intangible into a tangible objection you can actually handle.", "source": "objections/00-core-framework.md"}, {"id": "discount-request", "bucket": "financial", "type": "logistic", "label": "Are you offering any discounts?", "triggers": ["discount", "any discounts", "can you do better on price", "do anything on the price", "best you can do", "any deals", "anything cheaper", "knock the price down", "lower the price", "best price"], "response_steps": ["No. (There's nothing more you need to say than that. Don't do fast-action discounts or incentive-based pricing — they're a closing crutch and they cheapen the offer.)", "Quote the price as a flat statement and then go silent — 'the investment to get your business to [outcome] is just [price].' Do not fill the pause with a softener or a payment plan. Let the silence sit.", "If pressed, redirect to value, never to price: re-anchor the price to the outcome, and ask the binary — 'are you looking for the cheapest option, or a premium-quality option?' Keep the investment simple and fixed; payment terms (not discounts) are the only lever, and only after isolating a true financial objection."], "source": "objections/price-and-financial.md"}, {"id": "send-me-recording", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Send me the recording / a summary / email me and I'll review it", "triggers": ["send me the recording", "send the recording", "send me a summary", "email me the", "send me a recap", "send over the recording", "I'll review it", "review it on my own time", "go over it later"], "response_steps": ["No problem. Before I do that — let me ask you this: money and everything aside, do you feel like this is 100% what you need to get to [their goal], and that it's 100% going to work?", "Here's what I've found — a recording without me there to answer the questions that come up usually just sits there. So let's not let that happen to you. What's the real thing you'd be reviewing for — is there something specific you're still not sure about?", "If a real concern surfaces, that's the true objection — handle it. If there isn't one, don't book a loose follow-up: 'It sounds like you're 100% there. Let's just get you started — what's your billing address?'", "If they genuinely need a hard next step: lock a specific time tomorrow with a definitive tie-down — 'when we talk at [time], if you feel the same way, we're 100% moving forward, yes?'"], "do_not": "Don't treat this like 'think about it' and isolate certainty for ten minutes — and don't just send a recording into the void. This is the post-call-disappearance setup. Either close now or lock a hard, tied-down next step.", "source": "objections/think-about-it.md"}, {"id": "flat-exit", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I'll get back to you — flat exit / hand on the doorknob", "triggers": ["I'll get back to you", "let me get back to you", "I'll be in touch", "I'll reach out", "we'll let you know", "leave it with me", "I'll think it through and let you know"], "response_steps": ["Read the tonality. If they've clearly already decided and are just being polite, don't run another temp-check loop — use the honest takeaway.", "TAKEAWAY: 'Can I be totally straight with you? It feels like this is a no — and that's completely okay, I'd rather you tell me than disappear. Be honest with me: it's a no, isn't it?'", "This usually does one of two things — it either gets a real 'yes it's a no' (so you can ask the one question that surfaces the real reason: 'fair enough — what was the thing that didn't land?'), or it snaps them back: 'no, no, it's not that...' — and now the real objection is on the table.", "Whatever they name, handle it through diffuse -> isolate. Do not accept a vague exit."], "do_not": "Don't book a polite follow-up call you both know won't happen. A flat 'I'll get back to you' is a no being delivered gently — call it, with respect, so you get a real answer.", "source": "objections/think-about-it.md"}, {"id": "buyers-remorse", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Post-close cold feet / can I cancel / I'm not sure I should have done this", "triggers": ["can I cancel", "I want to cancel", "I changed my mind", "not sure I should have", "having second thoughts", "did I make the right", "want a refund", "regret this", "cold feet now"], "response_steps": ["Diffuse and stay calm — do not panic or get defensive: 'Totally hear you, and I'm glad you told me instead of sitting on it. Talk to me — what came up?'", "Re-anchor to why they bought: 'Earlier you told me [their goal / their pain] and that this was exactly what you needed. None of that changed in the last ten minutes — so what's actually going on right now?'", "Name it as nerves if that's what it is: 'This is the monkey brain doing its job — the moment after a big decision is when fear shouts loudest. That doesn't mean it was the wrong decision.'", "Re-confirm the decision and move them into action fast: 'Let's get you into onboarding right now and book your first call — momentum is what kills the doubt. You good?'"], "do_not": "Don't ignore post-close remorse hoping it passes, and don't immediately offer the refund. The deal isn't safe until cash clears and onboarding starts — reassure, re-anchor, and move them into action.", "source": "sales-process/03-committing-phase-and-closes.md"}]},
  discoveryFlags: {"version": "1.0", "description": "Discovery flags for the Call Copilot. During discovery, when the prospect says something that should be dug into, the app surfaces the flag + the exact probe question. Built from Cole Gordon's discovery methodology (the 7 beliefs: pain, doubt, cost, desire, money, support, trust).", "belief_prompts": {"pain": ["What's the single biggest challenge in the business right now? Or what's not working at the level it truly could be?", "Tell me more — when you said [that], what do you mean exactly? Why do you say that though?", "Has that put you in a tough position? In what way? How's it showing up day to day?"], "doubt": ["What have you already tried to fix this? What happened?", "When something like that doesn't work, it's usually one of two things — the method or the execution. Which do you think it was?", "What's been the single biggest thing keeping you from fixing this on your own?"], "cost": ["Can I ask you a personal question — what's your plan if nothing changes? What if the last five years are like the next five?", "If we roll forward 12 months and the business is still exactly here, what does that actually cost you — money, time, energy?", "What's it costing you right now to keep going the way you are?"], "desire": ["Where do you want the business to be? What's the revenue number you're driving toward, and why that number specifically?", "What would hitting that actually let you do — personally — that you can't do right now?", "Is there any other reason this is important to you now though?"], "money": ["Just for clarity — what was your exact revenue last month? And the month before?", "What's a single client worth to you over their lifetime?", "If this is the right move, is the budget there to make it happen — or would you need to free something up?"], "support": ["Who else is involved in a decision like this?", "Is your partner supportive of you making this change? Do they know you're on this call — what would they think if they knew?", "If your team has to implement this, do they have the bandwidth this quarter?"], "trust": ["What would make you 100% confident that we're the team to get you there?", "Have you looked at other options? What's drawing you to look at this now?", "Is there anything about working with us specifically you're unsure of — so I can clear it up now?"]}, "flags": [{"id": "vague-answer", "signal": "Vague or surface-level answer — they haven't really told you anything yet", "belief": "pain", "triggers": ["kind of", "sort of", "i guess", "things could be better", "a few things", "stuff like that", "here and there", "it's complicated", "hard to say", "a bit of everything"], "probe": "Tell me more — when you said [that], what do you mean exactly? Why do you say that though?", "note": "Don't move on. Paint the full portrait — repeat their last 3 words back as a question to get them to expand."}, {"id": "emotional-word", "signal": "They used an emotional word — there's real pain here, go deeper", "belief": "pain", "triggers": ["stressed", "stressful", "frustrated", "frustrating", "overwhelmed", "exhausted", "burnt out", "burned out", "worried", "anxious", "fed up", "sick of it", "drained", "miserable", "scared", "embarrassed", "ashamed", "struggling", "struggle", "i hate", "hopeless", "fed up with", "can't stand"], "probe": "Tell me more about that. Has that put you in a tough position? ... In what way though? How's that showing up for you?", "note": "Emotional words are gold — chase them. Get to the real, personal cost, not the surface."}, {"id": "names-a-number", "signal": "They named a specific goal/number — find out why THAT number", "belief": "desire", "triggers": ["i want to get to", "i want to hit", "my goal is", "k a month", "k per month", "grand a month", "k per year", "per year", "million", "figures", "seven figures", "i'd like to make"], "probe": "You seem like you've thought of that number before — can I ask, why that number? Why is that important to you? When do you want to hit it by?", "note": "A number with no 'why' behind it is shallow. Anchor it."}, {"id": "mentions-spouse", "signal": "They mentioned a spouse/partner — FLAG support; qualify it now, don't handle it", "belief": "support", "triggers": ["my wife", "my husband", "my spouse", "my partner", "my girlfriend", "my boyfriend", "my fiance", "talk to my wife", "my better half", "my significant other"], "probe": "Is your partner supportive of you fixing this? Are you guys on the same page about that problem? Does your partner know you're on this call — and what would they think if they knew?", "note": "Gather it now, naturally — do NOT handle a spouse objection in discovery. You'll need this later."}, {"id": "says-we", "signal": "They said 'we' / 'us' / 'the team' — there may be other decision-makers", "belief": "support", "triggers": ["we decided", "we want to", "we're looking", "we need to", "we both", "the two of us", "our team", "my business partner", "the partners", "my co-founder", "my co founder", "run it by the"], "probe": "When you say 'we' — who else is involved in a decision like this? Who would need to be comfortable with it if we decided it's the right move?", "note": "Surface every decision-maker early. A hidden one kills the close."}, {"id": "past-attempt", "signal": "They've tried something before — run solution questions, set up the pitch", "belief": "doubt", "triggers": ["i tried", "i've tried", "we tried", "i hired", "i bought", "i did a program", "i did a course", "signed up for", "invested in", "took a course", "worked with", "used an agency", "had a coach", "in the past i", "before i"], "probe": "What did you like or dislike about it? What was missing? When people go into something like that and don't get the result, it's usually one of two things — the method, or the execution. Which do you think it was?", "note": "This is your ammo. The pitch must explain why that failed and why this is different."}, {"id": "surface-goal-no-why", "signal": "They gave a goal but not the real reason behind it", "belief": "desire", "triggers": ["i want to grow", "i want more", "i want to scale", "want to make more", "want to be bigger", "the goal is to", "i'd love to"], "probe": "Why is that important to you? Why now though? And seeing as you're the founder — why is that important to you personally?", "note": "Use permission-reason-why for the deep personal reason: 'Can I ask a personal question? The reason I'm asking is...'"}, {"id": "stuck-long-time", "signal": "They've been stuck a long time — find the moment of decision", "belief": "cost", "triggers": ["for years", "a few years", "a couple years", "3 years", "5 years", "10 years", "a long time", "a while now", "for the longest time", "as long as i can remember", "always been", "still haven't", "keep trying", "been at this"], "probe": "Take me back to the last day you had that sudden realization that enough is enough — the day you decided to draw the line in the sand, step across it, burn the boats. Take me back to that day — what actually happened?", "note": "The moment of decision resurfaces the emotions of change. This is the highest-leverage discovery question."}, {"id": "no-pain", "signal": "They're downplaying, or money / pain isn't a lever — no clear problem surfaced", "belief": "pain", "triggers": ["things are okay", "things are fine", "things are good", "things are steady", "no real problems", "nothing major", "just looking", "just curious", "just exploring", "no real challenges", "can't complain", "not bad", "could be worse", "pretty good actually", "don't care about the money", "not about the money", "money isn't the issue", "money's not a concern", "money isn't a problem", "money is not an issue", "i don't really have a problem", "no real pain"], "probe": "On a scale of one to ten, where's [their area] at right now? ... And what does that number mean to you? ... If pain / money clearly isn't the lever (Matt Ryder): people don't book a call for no reason — what shifted recently that made NOW the time to look at this? Have you tried anything before, and why didn't it stick? Then measure the gap: how close does your current way realistically get you to [their goal]?", "note": "No problem, no sale. If the prospect downplays, run the 1-10 gap question. If they say money / pain isn't the issue, switch to the catalyst-event line — there is always a reason they got on the call; the gap between their current method and their goal IS the urgency."}, {"id": "story-not-numbers", "signal": "They're telling a story instead of giving you numbers", "belief": "pain", "triggers": ["so basically", "what happened was", "let me explain", "it's a long story", "so the thing is", "honestly it's been"], "probe": "Got it — let's get specific. Last week exactly, how many [leads/calls/sales]? What about the week before? What was your exact revenue last month?", "note": "People tell stories about their problems; the truth is in the numbers. Chunk down."}, {"id": "mentions-competitor", "signal": "They mentioned a competitor or other option — FLAG, note it, don't chase now", "belief": "trust", "triggers": ["another company", "another option", "looking at other", "talking to", "i saw another", "comparing", "other quotes", "shopping around"], "probe": "(Note it — don't handle it in discovery.) Later, at the close: 'Price aside, which are you more certain can actually get you there?'", "note": "Don't reframe in discovery. Flush it out, save it for the transition/objections."}, {"id": "asks-price-early", "signal": "They're pushing to price before discovery is done", "belief": "none", "triggers": ["what's the price", "how much is it", "how much does it cost", "what's the investment", "just tell me the price", "what are we talking", "ballpark"], "probe": "Everything we do is customized — so the most time-efficient thing is to get a little context first, then I can share the parts relevant to you. Is that fair?", "note": "Don't drop the price early. Redirect to discovery. Pricing before value = lost deal."}, {"id": "logistics-question", "signal": "They asked a logistics question — there may be a hidden objection under it", "belief": "trust", "triggers": ["is it group", "is this group coaching", "how long is the program", "how does it work", "do i get one on one", "is it one on one", "how often do we meet", "what's included"], "probe": "There are elements of [X] — but just so I can answer your question correctly, is there a specific reason you're asking?", "note": "Never answer a logistics question flat. The reason behind it is usually the real objection."}, {"id": "deadline-pressure", "signal": "They mentioned a deadline or external pressure — that's cost/urgency", "belief": "cost", "triggers": ["by the end of the year", "by next year", "my wife said", "my husband said", "running out of", "if i don't", "or else", "have to figure this out", "can't keep going like this"], "probe": "What happens if nothing changes? If we roll this forward 90 days and you're still dealing with the same thing — what gets harder, what stays off the table?", "note": "This is the cost-of-inaction lever. Dig the consequence, then ladder deeper."}, {"id": "uncertain-tonality", "signal": "They're hedging — uncertainty you'll need to clear at the temp check", "belief": "trust", "triggers": ["i think so", "i guess so", "i'm not sure", "maybe", "we'll see", "possibly", "i suppose", "i hope so"], "probe": "(Note the hedge.) At the temp check, push for certainty: 'Do you think this is 100% going to work? Do you 100% want to do this?'", "note": "A hedge now becomes an objection at the close. Flag it."}, {"id": "owner-trapped-in-delivery", "signal": "The owner is stuck working IN the business — trapped in delivery / the day-to-day", "belief": "desire", "triggers": ["in the weeds", "working in the business", "on the business", "doing everything myself", "can't step back", "can't take a day off", "wearing every hat", "i am the business", "trapped in", "stuck in the day to day", "no time off"], "probe": "What would the business look like if you weren't in the day-to-day of it? ... If this freed you from [that part], what would you actually do with that time — and what would it mean for the business to run without you in the engine room?", "note": "For a business owner the real desire is usually leverage — getting out of delivery, not out of a job. Tie the goal to what their time gets reinvested into."}, {"id": "fear-risk-word", "signal": "They voiced a fear or risk — chase it now, it becomes the nerves objection later", "belief": "doubt", "triggers": ["nervous", "scared", "afraid", "what if it doesn't work", "worried it won't", "big leap", "burned before", "been burned"], "probe": "Tell me more about that — what specifically worries you? Why do you say that though?", "note": "A voiced fear in discovery is the doubt belief surfacing early. Chase the emotional word now to understand it — but don't fully HANDLE it as the nerves objection until the committing phase."}, {"id": "mentions-family-lifestyle", "signal": "They mentioned kids/family/lifestyle — tie the goal to the personal payoff", "belief": "desire", "triggers": ["my kids", "my family", "my children", "more time", "freedom", "lifestyle", "be present", "my daughter", "my son", "retire my", "for my family"], "probe": "Can I ask you a personal question? The reason I'm asking is we want this to work around your lifestyle goals — so what are the personal goals you want your business to allow you to achieve?", "note": "The strongest sales tie the monetary goal to a non-monetary, personal one."}, {"id": "contradiction", "signal": "They contradicted something they said earlier — flag it for the loop", "belief": "none", "triggers": ["now that i think about it", "what i meant was", "on second thought", "well actually", "come to think of it", "i take that back"], "probe": "(Note the contradiction.) Later: 'Earlier you said [X], but now you're saying [Y] — what's really going on?'", "note": "Their own words are the most powerful tool to handle a later objection."}, {"id": "rambling", "signal": "Long rambling answer — cut in, redirect, get specific", "belief": "none", "triggers": ["anyway", "i don't know if that makes sense", "long story short", "to make a long story"], "probe": "Got it — let me make sure I understand. So the main thing is [their core point], right? Let's dig into that specifically.", "note": "Don't let discovery sprawl. Stay in the lead, get to the gap."}, {"id": "busy-no-time", "signal": "They mentioned being busy / no time — probe priorities now, it'll become an objection later", "belief": "cost", "triggers": ["i'm so busy", "i'm really busy", "no time", "don't have time", "swamped", "stretched thin", "too much on my plate", "wearing all the hats"], "probe": "If [their constraint] is the #1 thing holding the business back — why wouldn't fixing it be your #1 priority? If not now, when?", "note": "Pre-empt the 'no time to implement' objection by anchoring priorities here."}, {"id": "misdiagnosis", "signal": "They've named a problem — but make sure it's the REAL constraint", "belief": "doubt", "triggers": ["the problem is", "my biggest issue is", "what i need is", "i just need more", "if i could just"], "probe": "What do you think has been the biggest thing keeping you from fixing that on your own? What's in the way?", "note": "Prospects often misdiagnose. Probe the real constraint before agreeing with their diagnosis."}, {"id": "doubt-themselves", "signal": "They expressed doubt (or overconfidence) about doing it alone — the doubt belief", "belief": "doubt", "triggers": ["i could probably do it myself", "i should be able to", "i just haven't", "i know what to do i just", "i could figure it out"], "probe": "If you could've done it on your own, you probably would have by now — so what's actually been in the way? What's been the hardest part?", "note": "Address why a proven path beats DIY: less time, energy, and risk to the result."}, {"id": "real-reason-because", "signal": "They gave you a real reason — anchor it, then go one level deeper", "belief": "desire", "triggers": ["the real reason", "if i'm being honest", "to be honest with you", "what really gets me", "deep down", "what really bothers me", "if i'm honest", "truthfully", "the truth is", "what it really comes down to"], "probe": "I guess that makes sense — is there any other reason this is important to you now though?", "note": "The 'any other reason' question often surfaces the truest, most emotional driver. Everyone has two reasons — the one that sounds good and the real one."}, {"id": "money-tightness", "signal": "They mentioned money/cash being tight — install the money belief NOW, in discovery", "belief": "money", "triggers": ["things are tight", "money is tight", "cash flow", "cash is tight", "can't really afford", "tight on money", "tight financially", "strapped", "running low on cash", "money's been tight"], "probe": "Has that put you in a tough position financially — in what way though? ... Is that a revenue problem, or is it more about where the money's going right now?", "note": "Surface and install the money belief in discovery — a financial-tightness comment now, left alone, becomes a price objection at the close. Installing the money belief in discovery creates the consistency that eliminates the financial objection later."}, {"id": "cost-of-inaction", "signal": "Long-running problem or a goal with no urgency — install the cost belief", "belief": "cost", "triggers": ["if nothing changes", "stay the same", "keep going like this", "same as last year", "another year of", "if this carries on", "where i've always been", "stuck where i am"], "probe": "Can I ask you another personal question — and I really hate to ask this — but what's your plan if nothing changes? What if the last five years are like the next five years?", "note": "The cost-of-inaction lever. This is Cole's single most-repeated cost question — it makes the prospect feel the price of standing still."}, {"id": "lead-volume-no-fit", "signal": "They talk lead/revenue volume without qualifying fit — probe ICP quality", "belief": "doubt", "triggers": ["i get leads", "we get leads", "plenty of leads", "lots of leads", "i get traffic", "get enquiries", "get inquiries", "i get some leads"], "probe": "Out of those leads, how many actually fit the exact ideal client you want to attract? ... Let's get specific — what was your exact revenue last month? What about the month before? Is that gross or net?", "note": "Chunk down to numbers. The real problem is often lead QUALITY, not volume — and stories hide it, numbers reveal it."}]},
  funnel: {"version": "1.0", "description": "The 6-stage sales call funnel for the Call Copilot stage tracker. Each stage gives the rep the goal, what to listen for, the verbatim lines to say, and when to advance. Sourced from MASTER-SALES-SCRIPT.md and sales-process/.", "stages": [{"id": "introduction", "name": "1. Introduction", "goal": "Open with rapport, acknowledge the lead source + pain from triage, surface the outcome they want from this call, confirm the nudge they want to work with us, then future-pace into discovery.", "listen_for": "Energy + tonality. The nudge — anything that says they want help / want to move forward. If they're flat or distracted, reposition before pushing on.", "advance_when": "You've ticked 'Nudge confirmed' (above) and they've named the outcome they want / their biggest challenge — then move to Discovery.", "options": [{"id": "primary", "title": "Option A — Conversational (you already have notes / triage info)", "lines": ["[Name] — tell me about your day.", "(Acknowledge where they came from and their pain.) So before we get into that — what do you want to have happen by the end of this meeting? What's an ideal outcome for you?", "Assuming you get all of that, what happens next in your world?"]}, {"id": "alternate", "title": "Option B — Frame-first (you don't have much prospect info)", "lines": ["Hello [name]! Can you hear me OK? See me OK? ... Awesome. Lovely to meet you, I'm [you]. I have your notes here, looking forward to diving into everything.", "I see we have the call scheduled for 45 minutes — just wanted to see how much time you have, or if you have a set dead stop? ... OK awesome.", "So FIRST let's dive deep into the specifics of your business and how you're using social media. So let's talk about what's working right now, what's not working right now, and ultimately the specific challenges or constraints that are keeping you from where you want to be. And then once we get some clarity there, if we can help, I'll dive into what we have going on over here. Sound good?", "So probably our best place to start — what would you say your biggest challenge is right now? Or at least, what's not working at the level it truly feels like it could or should be? (If they don't name one: what prompted you to respond and get on this call with me?)"]}]}, {"id": "discovery", "name": "2. Discovery", "goal": "Understand IF and HOW you can help. Cover the 7 beliefs (pain, doubt, cost, desire, money, support, trust). Eliminate objections before the close.", "listen_for": "Discovery flags — vague answers, emotional words, numbers, spouse/team mentions, past attempts, hedging. The copilot will surface probes.", "say": ["What's your biggest challenge right now? Or what's not working at the level it truly could be?", "CATALYST (Matt Ryder — use when there's no obvious pain, e.g. they say money isn't the issue): People don't book a call for no reason. So what shifted recently that made NOW the time to look at this? ... Have you tried anything before — and why didn't it stick? (If they give a surface answer, loop: aside from that, what about it actually spoke to you?) Then measure the gap: with your current way of doing it, how close does that realistically get you to [their goal]? — that gap is the urgency.", "Tell me more — when you said [X], what do you mean exactly? Why do you say that though?", "Has that put you in a tough position? ... And in what way though? (Curious tone — chase the cost, don't move on.)", "Tell me about the business — what do you sell, who's it for, and how long have you been running it? ... What part of running it drains you the most right now?", "Take me back to the moment you realised the way you'd been growing this wasn't going to get you where you want — what was going on in the business that made you decide enough is enough?", "Last week specifically, how many [leads / sales calls] did you generate? What about the week before? Out of those, how many fit the exact ideal client you want? ... Just for clarity — what was your exact revenue last month? What about the month before?", "MATH (Ravi client value — lock these for the upside math): What's a single client worth to you over their lifetime? On average, how many clients do you close a month? (Tick the 'Math (Ravi LTV)' chip above when you've captured this.)", "So you're making [guess] a month right now then, correct?", "Begin with the end in mind — ultimately, where do you want the business to be? What's the revenue number you're driving toward, and what would the business look like at that point? Why that number specifically?", "Can I ask another personal question — and I really hate to ask this — but what's your plan if nothing changes? What if the last five years are like the next five years?", "I guess that makes sense — is there any other reason this is important to you now though?", "Can I ask a personal question? The reason I'm asking is we want this to work around your lifestyle goals — what are the personal goals you want your business to allow you to achieve?", "What else have you tried to fix this? What did you like or dislike about it? What we've found is when people don't get the result, it's one of two things — [blank] or [blank]. Which do you think it was?", "Are you married? Is your partner supportive of the change? Do they know you're on this call — and what would they think if they knew?"], "advance_when": "You're 100% clear on their biggest challenge AND their real desire — business and personal. Not surface-level."}, {"id": "transition", "name": "3. Transition", "goal": "Move from questions to pitch with zero sales resistance — get the prospect to ask you to pitch them.", "listen_for": "Confirmation they feel understood.", "say": ["I don't think I have any more questions — is there anything else you feel like we haven't covered that you feel like I need to know?", "Based on what you've told me, we can definitely help.", "Cool — and there are 3 things that you're going to do, whether you work with me or not, to go from [where they are now] to [where they want to be]. So where do you want to go from here? I can walk you through what those 3 things are and how we'd do it together if you want — but you tell me where you want to go."], "advance_when": "They ask you to walk them through it."}, {"id": "pitch", "name": "4. Pitch", "goal": "Sell the METHOD, not the deliverables. High-level promise -> 3 pillars -> delivery. Each pillar is the simultaneous explanation of why their past attempts failed and why this is different. Tie-down after every pillar.", "listen_for": "Comprehension. If they say 'yeah' but clearly don't get it — stop and re-explain. Pillars 1 & 2 are paradigm shifts; 3 is the payoff.", "say": ["Gotcha. Do you have your pen and pad? Great — on your pen and pad, write out one through three (or four), with a good amount of space in between.", "Let me preface this by saying — everything we do for clients is all customised, based on what's best for the client. For you specifically, it's going to be three things, three things to help you go from [current state they said] to [desired state they said].", "Now before I go over all the details, can I just ask you for a favour? ... Great — because we believe a healthy relationship begins with healthy communication. So while I may sound direct, it's because that'll allow you to get what you need to get [outcome] working. Is that fair enough? And on the other hand, I'll ask the same of you.", "These calls go one of three ways. One, yes, it's amazing, I want to work with you guys. Two, no, it's not the right fit — and I want to let you know in advance it's totally okay if you say no to me, you won't hurt my feelings. But the third thing I want to stay away from is the maybe, the 'let me sleep on it', because a lot of the time that's just a polite way to say no. Does that sound fair enough?", "Have you been to Japan? ... So a while back I was on a trip in Japan, and I was super hungry — and I'll be honest with you, when I get hungry I do get a little hangry. So I was walking down the street with my family but I couldn't figure out what any of the restaurants were offering — even though they had tons of big, bold menus and signs outside — because Japanese is a language I don't understand. And it reminded me of this: the same thing is happening in your marketing right now. You could be spending tens of thousands more per month on ads, or posting content 10 times a day, but because your expertise isn't being communicated in a way your ideal client understands, it feels like you're speaking to them in a foreign language. So even if you put in more effort and time right now, it won't result in additional revenue. So — the first thing we're going to do for you is give you the right social media strategy, to make sure you're speaking in the right language, so your value is communicated in a way the right people understand and want. Are you following me so far?", "Great — and what's your schedule looking like over the next few days? ... Fantastic. So, should you decide to move forward on this call, I'll get Lauren to create your strategy for you — she'll look into your brand and tap into the psychology of your best possible client to identify the right platforms, content style and positioning for you. Then Mariana, who's run my socials for the last half-decade, will personally deliver it to you on a 1:1 call where you can ask her anything you'd like. Looking at her calendar, we can make [date] or [date] work — which suits you best? ... Fantastic. So what questions do you have about that part, specifically?", "[Name], you seem pretty in shape — do you go to the gym, or what exercise do you do? ... So you know there are some people you see in the gym every time, always running on the treadmill, but they just don't seem to change body shape? They don't know what to do, what to eat outside the gym, so they get zero results — have you seen those people? ... Right. And there are also people who go to the gym only 3 times, stay just 30-40 minutes, and because they have a strategy on how to train and systems around what to eat, despite putting in less effort they're in amazing shape. That's the difference between just posting on social media, and posting with our AI Content System. It's how we get more than 100,000 views organically per week across our socials — but more importantly, how we drive revenue from social media. Do you see my posts a lot? ... Yep — someone who joined us last week, whose business was previously dependent on ads, booked 3 sales calls within 24 hours of starting with us. Because the AI Content System is based on all the data we've gathered from sharing 200,000+ of our own posts, and millions more on behalf of our clients. What used to take us 3 months and $25,000 to teach people, we can now hand to you at the click of a button. So we'll actually build this out FOR you — meaning you're left with an AI system that writes all your content for the week, specifically in your voice, so your accounts aren't just reaching more people, but your content results in real revenue. What do you feel that would do for your business? ... Does that make sense? What questions do you have about that specifically?", "Now imagine this. We're six weeks in the future and we've attracted all of your ideal clients here — and, can you see my hand? ... And you're over here on an island with the solution to what they want. No matter how big the traffic is, or how good your solution is — if there isn't a bridge connecting the two, they can't buy and work with you. There might be a couple of people who swim across, but you're losing out on the majority if you don't have a solid bridge. So that's why the last thing we'll do is give you the bridge — so you're left with prequalified prospects who are ready to buy."], "advance_when": "You've covered all 3 pillars with a tie-down after each. Then run the conservative upside math and move to Committing."}, {"id": "committing", "name": "5. Committing Phase", "goal": "Get them 100% bought in on the thesis BEFORE money is on the table. Temp check -> onboarding -> price drop.", "say": ["QUESTIONS: What questions do you have about those [3] things specifically?", "UPSIDE MATH: Quick bit of math so this isn't abstract. You told me a client is worth about [LTV] to you. If this system just gets you one more client a month from organic — content you otherwise wouldn't even have posted — that's [LTV x 12] in extra revenue over the next 12 months. And that's the conservative version, just one more client a month.", "SMALL TEMP: So based on you telling me you want to get to [outcome] — do you feel like this is what you've been looking for?", "HARD TEMP (scale 1-10): What's really important to us is alignment — when you come and work with us, we're rolling up the sleeves, getting in the trenches with you, and our team is all in. So just to be 100% clear, on a scale of one to ten, one being 'I hate this guy, get me off the phone,' ten being 'that's exactly what I need' — where do you fall out exactly? ... What's keeping you from being a nine or a ten? (8 or under: 'why so low?' → handle → re-ask. No 7s.)", "TRANSITION: So you feel really good about the process, no questions — what's next, where do you want to go from here?", "ONBOARDING (before price): Basically, next steps — you'll process the investment with me. Once we take care of that, we set up an onboarding call, give you some homework, and lay out when we're going to meet, how often, what we'll give you and what we need from you — so you have complete clarity and certainty on exactly what's going to happen over the next 12 weeks. Does that sound good?", "PRICE DROP: And the next steps are very simple — the investment is just [X].", "CLOSE: How do you feel? ... You sure? ... Ready to get started on some homework? ... What's your billing address?"], "listen_for": "Tonality on the temp check. 'Dude, absolutely' = yes. 'I think so' = no. Price drop: soft, downward inflection — the price ends the sentence on a period, then go quiet (not a Mexican standoff).", "advance_when": "After the price drop + close attempt, the prospect stalls or raises an objection. (If they say yes through the close, the sale is done — skip the Objections stage.)"}, {"id": "objections", "name": "6. Objections", "goal": "Diffuse -> isolate -> handle uncertainty before logistics -> re-tie-down -> close. Loop until they're 100% in.", "say": ["STEP 1 — DIFFUSE: No problem.", "STEP 2 — ISOLATE: Just so I can stay organized — when you say [objection], are you more in a 'should I do this' place where you're not 100% certain this is what you want, or a 'how can I do this' place where you're certain and it's just logistics?", "STEP 3 — TEMP CHECK: [Objection] aside — how do you feel about the process? Do you feel this is 100% what you need to get to [outcome], and that it's 100% going to work?", "STEP 4 — SCALE: On a scale of 1 to 10 — one being 'get me off the phone', ten being 'that's exactly what I need' — where do you fall exactly? ... What's keeping you from a 9 or 10?", "STEP 5 — DOUBLE TIE-DOWN: So [objection] aside — is there anything else keeping you from being less than 100% certain this is the right thing AND now is the right time? ... So you're 100% in?", "If the tonality is off and the stated objection feels like a cover: For real, I can tell there's something. So what's really going on? What's really coming up for you?", "Then handle the specific objection. Trade every concession for a decision: 'If I'm willing to do that for you, are you willing to move forward right now?'"], "listen_for": "Which objection. Handle uncertainty before money/support/timing — a logistic handled while uncertainty is unresolved is a smoke screen. Should-I = uncertainty (handle the belief); How-can-I = logistic (trade and close). On the scale: 8 or under, ask 'why so low?', handle, re-ask. No 7s.", "advance_when": "They're 100% in and you've closed — move to Close Confirmation to button down the sale."}, {"id": "close-confirmation", "name": "7. Close Confirmation", "goal": "Button down the sale. Restate next steps, reassure, pre-frame against buyer's remorse, start onboarding momentum. The deal isn't safe until cash clears and onboarding begins.", "listen_for": "Hesitation, second thoughts, a tone shift after the card is processed — post-close remorse. If it appears, handle it (see the buyers-remorse objection) — don't go silent.", "say": ["Awesome — congratulations, this is a big move and I'm genuinely excited for you. Here's exactly what happens next: [restate the onboarding steps + first call date].", "Real quick — right after a big decision like this, your brain might get loud and try to second-guess it. That's totally normal, it's the monkey brain doing its job. It doesn't mean it was the wrong call — it means it mattered. If anything comes up, you call me directly, okay?", "Let's get your onboarding form done right now while we're together, and get your first call on the calendar — momentum is what makes this work.", "You made a great decision. I've got your back — anytime you need anything, you reach out. Let's go get you [their outcome]."], "advance_when": "Payment has cleared, onboarding form is done, and the first call is booked. The sale is complete."}]}
};
